{
  "id": "hiskia",
  "name": "Hezekiah",
  "title": "The Reforming King",
  "era": "divided-kingdom",
  "lifespan": "c. 739–687 BC",
  "summary": "Hezekiah was one of Judah's most godly kings. He carried out extensive religious reforms, reopened the temple, and celebrated Passover for the first time in a long while. When the Assyrian king Sennacherib besieged Jerusalem, Hezekiah trusted in God, and an angel struck down the Assyrian army. God also granted him 15 additional years of life when he was mortally ill.",
